    "visibleText": "Designer \nwho \nships \nwith \nvision\nDesign  Engineer who ships growth\n\nI'm Andreas, making precise, joyful interfaces and the tools to build them, from first sketch to production so that your team ships and your business grows.\n\nWork\nCheval\nInbox\nCanvas\nArrange\nShare\n\n2. Inbox: crit and variants\n\nInbox\nBrief\nA\nCheval Lab\nInbox\nImportant\n7,613\nDrafts\n2\nSent\nAgent\nAll\nGitHub\n10:38\nNotes from today's workshop\nFigma\n10:33\nReceipt for your payment\nKenji Sato\n10:06\nSecurity alert\nVercel\n09:44\nShared a file with you\nMaren Vos\n09:37\nDraft for the launch post\nTomasz Nowak\n09:31\nFeedback on the prototype\nNo thread selected\nOpen the latest thread\nA: Dense list\nA\nCheval Lab\nInbox\nImportant\n7,613\nDrafts\n2\nSent\nAgent\nAll\nToday\nG\nGitHub\n10:38\nNotes from today's workshop\nF\nFigma\n10:33\nReceipt for your payment\nK\nKenji Sato\n10:06\nSecurity alert\nV\nVercel\n09:44\nShared a file with you\nM\nMaren Vos\n09:37\nDraft for the launch post\nT\nTomasz Nowak\n09:31\nFeedback on the prototype\nNo thread selected\nOpen the latest thread\nA v2: Grouped by day\nA\nCheval Lab\nInbox\nImportant\n7,613\nDrafts\n2\nSent\nAgent\nAll\nToday\nG\nGitHub\n10:38\nNotes from today's workshop\nF\nFigma\n10:33\nReceipt for your payment\nK\nKenji Sato\n10:06\nSecurity alert\nV\nVercel\n09:44\nShared a file with you\nM\nMaren Vos\n09:37\nDraft for the launch post\nT\nTomasz Nowak\n09:31\nFeedback on the prototype\nNo thread selected\nOpen the latest thread\nA v3: Unread first\n\n3. Inbox at three widths\n\nA\nCheval Lab\nInbox\nImportant\n7,613\nDrafts\n2\nSent\nAgent\nAll\nToday\nG\nGitHub\n10:38\nNotes from today's workshop\nF\nFigma\n10:33\nReceipt for your payment\nK\nKenji Sato\n10:06\nSecurity alert\nV\nVercel\n09:44\nShared a file with you\nM\nMaren Vos\n09:37\nDraft for the launch post\nT\nTomasz Nowak\n09:31\nFeedback on the prototype\nNo thread selected\nOpen the latest thread\nInbox v12, 1440\nAll\nToday\nG\nGitHub\n10:38\nNotes from today's workshop\nF\nFigma\n10:33\nReceipt for your payment\nK\nKenji Sato\n10:06\nSecurity alert\nV\nVercel\n09:44\nShared a file with you\nM\nMaren Vos\n09:37\nDraft for the launch post\nT\nTomasz Nowak\n09:31\nFeedback on the prototype\nNo thread selected\nOpen the latest thread\nInbox v12, 810\nAll\nToday\nG\nGitHub\n10:38\nNotes from today's workshop\nF\nFigma\n10:33\nReceipt for your payment\nK\nKenji Sato\n10:06\nSecurity alert\nV\nVercel\n09:44\nShared a file with you\nM\nMaren Vos\n09:37\nDraft for the launch post\nT\nTomasz Nowak\n09:31\nFeedback on the prototype\nP\nPriya Raman\n09:08\nQuick question about the pricing page\nJ\nJoris De Wit\n08:26\nDesign review moved to Thursday\nInbox v12, 390\nView\nDesign tool\nDesign engineering\nAI\nProduct prototyping made 90% faster and more traceable for teamwork\nCheval Studio, my own prototyping tool\nEcoStruxure EMS\nGreen hydrogen plant\nEnergy flows\nSLD\nH₂ / NH₃\nForecast\nEnergy\nKPI\nStatus\nSettings\nOnline\nO1\nOperator 1\nSupply\n205.90 MW\n+3.1%\nElectrolyzers\n95.23 MW\n+0.4%\nH₂ output\n2,000 kg/h\n+1.8%\nH₂ stored\n2,000 kg\n+0.6%\nAlarms\n0 none active\nUtility\n200 MW\nSolar\n0.40 MW\nWind\n5.20 MW\nSolar\n0.30 MW\nBattery\n0.00 MW\nSoC\n92%\n57.14 MW\nStack 1\n3 of 3 running\nElectrolyzers\n95%\n1A\n19.05 MW\n36.3 Nm³/h\n95%\n1B\n19.05 MW\n36.3 Nm³/h\n95%\n1C\n19.04 MW\n36.3 Nm³/h\n38.09 MW\nStack 2\n2 of 2 running\nElectrolyzers\n95%\n2A\n19.05 MW\n36.3 Nm³/h\n95%\n2B\n19.04 MW\n36.3 Nm³/h\nH₂ compressor and storage\n13.26 MW\n350 bar\nClosed\nOpen\nNH₃ production\n19.20 MW\n270 kg/h\nView\nProduct design\nData visualisation\nEnergy\nA dashboard redesign that made $172M in 3 weeks\nSchneider Electric, ADIPEC\nBuilt to move\n\nLike the horse, I work best in motion. With the teams I work with, I find the clear way through and build the tools that get us there. Here's how that crossing works.\n\nHow I design\nBeyond\nwork\n\nAlways moving, rarely alone. Hosting design nights, ambassador work for SpaceXSI and Mobbin, and many many laughs in between ;)\n\nMore about me\nTaste notes\n\nWriting on design, culture, and how I view the world.\n\nMore writing\n2026-11\nThe\ncooldown\n07\n2026-10\nNouns,\nthen verbs\n06\n2026-10\nWhich\nexit\n05\n2026-10\nHidden\nsystem\n04\nSmall talk\n\nThe short ones are here. For anything else, ask the cloud.\n\nHow did you get into design?\n\nI've loved sci-fi and tech since I was a kid, and my favourite game was Minecraft. That's where I learned to think in systems: a few simple blocks, and rules you can build anything from.\n\nAt 17 I wanted to build my own, so I tried to learn Swift from a tutorial. The app it built was pastel shapes with drop shadows, and I couldn't stand it, so I redesigned it before I'd finished learning the code. Looking for how an interface should look, I found a design community online that didn't know my name. I felt part of it anyway, and I stayed.\n\nWhat's your main thing?\n\nDesign first, then the system underneath, in code. I make founders' products easy to get, so customers buy and investors say yes.\n\nHonestly, I'm more of a people person than a design person. Design is the best excuse I've found to get what's in someone's head out where everyone can see it, and then argue about the spacing.\n\nWhere are you based?\n\nCurrently based in Seoul \n. Before that, five years in The Hague in the Netherlands, and originally from a small village in Poland.\n\nWhere do you see yourself in the future?\n\nSomewhere fast and lively, San Francisco could be great, at a startup I believe in, with a GOATed team. Getting as good at the craft as I can, and building the community with designers in my spare time: events, dinners and some fun hangouts.\n\nOutside the 12-hour workdays, some time for art, and of course lots of running ;)\n\nHow can I get in touch?\n\nBook a call from the bar, or email andreaskruszakin@gmail.com. Tell me what you're building and where it's hard to get. I write back.\n\nAnd if your question isn't up here, ask the cloud. I hate talking about myself, so I taught it to do that for me.\n\nAndreas Kruszakin-Liboska\nLinkedIn\nX\nGitHub\nInstagram\nandreaskruszakin@gmail.com\nWork\nAbout\nWriting\nPlay\nWrocław, PL\n14:45\nGMT+1\nThe Hague, NL\n14:45\nGMT+1\nSan Francisco, US\n05:45\nGMT-8\nWork\nAbout\nWriting\nPlay\nClose\nBook a call",
